WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:03.730
Aya, the truth is...

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:06.770
I'm not actually English.

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:07.750
What?

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:10.860
I'm 100% Japanese, too.

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:11.990
What?

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:14.720
O-Oh, come on...

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:16.740
I dye my hair,

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:19.040
and wear color contacts.

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:21.090
Wh-What?

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:24.240
I've never been a natural blonde.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:26.510
Alice sounds serious!

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:28.420
You're joking, right?

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:29.630
Just kidding!

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:32.260
Successful Prank

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:31.430
Ta-da!

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:35.010
Successful Prank

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:33.280
Huh?

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:08.010
April Fool's?

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:10.220
April Ayaya!

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:12.800
But the new semester's already started.

00:02:13.630 --> 00:02:16.480
April 1st was a long time ago.

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:23.230
You're So Bright

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:18.150
Don't scare me like that.

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:21.400
It's not April Fool's Day.

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:23.320
It's Pretend April Fool's Day.

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:25.150
Pretend?

00:02:25.150 --> 00:02:28.520
I didn't tell enough lies on April 1st,

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:30.290
so I want to tell them now.

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:34.380
Apparently, April Fool's Day
is a lot of fun in England.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:36.870
Even their newspapers feature fake articles.

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:39.960
English people love jokes.

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:42.440
What should I do? What should I do?

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:46.090
Is something wrong, miss?

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:48.520
I've lost my watch.

00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:50.340
What time is it?

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:53.680
If you need to know the time...

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:54.480
What?

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:58.730
Oh, of course. There's always Big Ben.

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:04.190
What?

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:07.490
Is that true?

00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:09.190
It's true.

00:03:09.190 --> 00:03:11.870
They said it on BBC.

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:13.820
On BBC?

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:17.130
What kind of country is England, anyway?

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:18.370
It's amazing.

00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:23.130
B-But you can't lie on days that aren't April 1st.

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:26.610
If you lie, the god Yama
will tear your tongue out.

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:27.410
What?

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:29.130
M-My tongue?

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:32.010
Th-That's a lie!

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:35.210
You're lying now, Ayaya! That's not fair!

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:37.270
It's just a saying.

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:40.280
Lying is definitely bad.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:43.150
It's okay once a year, but...

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:45.970
Is something wrong?

00:03:45.970 --> 00:03:48.370
My younger brother and sister tell lies

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:52.010
that are hard to tell if they're lies or not.

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:54.160
They're just in fourth grade.

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:56.160
They're liars?

00:03:56.470 --> 00:03:59.660
Yeah. They're famous for it at school.

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:02.010
Their teachers and friends

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:04.420
call them the "Fibbing Brothers."

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:08.000
I'm kinda jealous!

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.160
You're jealous?

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:10.920
It sounds like a band name!

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:14.120
Oh! You have siblings, Youko?

00:04:14.830 --> 00:04:16.730
A younger brother and sister.

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:18.450
I've never met them.

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:21.870
Kouta-kun and Mitsuki-chan are twins.

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:23.940
I met them when they were little.

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:26.910
I wish I had siblings.

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:29.380
If I were an older sister...

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:34.950
Youko, you're their older sister!
You should discipline them!

00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:36.870
Discipline them?

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:37.910
Older
Sister
Wind

00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:38.830
<i>Where did this wind come from?</i>

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:40.830
Tell them, "Don't lie!"

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:41.710
Whoa!

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:44.480
Not "whoa." It's "no!"

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:45.710
What are you doing here?

00:04:45.710 --> 00:04:47.480
Huh? What—

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:48.960
Huh?!

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:51.200
I'm Inokuma Kouta.

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:52.220
I'm Mitsuki.

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:54.780
We transferred here today.

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:56.950
We're in the grade below you.

00:04:56.950 --> 00:04:58.530
Nice to meet you.

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:00.350
Don't lie so naturally!

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:02.450
They're so cute.

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:06.740
I-If you keep staring, we'll explode.

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:07.610
We will.

00:05:07.610 --> 00:05:09.200
E-Explode?

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:12.110
<i>I don't think they're liars...</i>

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:14.610
<i>They're just shy.</i>

00:05:14.920 --> 00:05:17.390
What are you doing at the high school?

00:05:17.390 --> 00:05:19.550
Didn't you have classes this morning?

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:21.170
We forgot our key.

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:23.050
Mom and Dad are at work.

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:26.190
I still have another hour of classes.

00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:28.250
Take my key and go home.

00:05:28.250 --> 00:05:28.970
Here.

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:30.900
It's okay, we'll wait.

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:34.800
When we told the nurse,
she said we could wait here.

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:36.180
That was sneaky!

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:38.680
We were in tears when we asked her.

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:40.570
They were fake tears, even?!

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:40.930
Eye Drops

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:43.350
My name is Karen.

00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:45.050
I'm Shinobu.

00:05:45.050 --> 00:05:46.350
Do you remember me?

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:47.960
I'm Aya.

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:51.000
Thanks for showing kindness to our older sister.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:52.830
They're so mature.

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:56.070
I'm Alice. Nice to meet you.

00:05:59.190 --> 00:06:00.870
Nice to meet you, Alice-chan.

00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:04.160
Hey! Alice is my age!

00:06:04.540 --> 00:06:06.130
Unbelievable.

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:09.190
They came to see you because they
were lonely. Go easy on them.

00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:11.020
Y-You're wrong.

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:14.170
We don't even like our older sister.

00:06:14.170 --> 00:06:15.840
We just forgot our key.

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:19.820
R-Really?

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:21.940
But...

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:25.980
I love you guys!

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:26.600
Youko!

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:31.540
We'd better head back to class.

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:32.820
You guys go on ahead.

00:06:33.150 --> 00:06:36.220
I'll take the kids to the nurse's office.

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:38.910
We'll come get you after class.

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:40.170
Wait for us.

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:41.120
Okay.

00:06:41.950 --> 00:06:47.120
Nurse's Office

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:44.350
This is it.

00:06:44.350 --> 00:06:46.040
Thank you.

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:47.120
What you said was

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:48.470
a lie, wasn't it?

00:06:49.490 --> 00:06:50.380
Huh?

00:06:52.130 --> 00:06:54.730
I know how you feel.

00:06:54.730 --> 00:06:55.380
Wha—

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:57.010
Where did this come from?

00:06:57.770 --> 00:07:00.520
You were lying when you said
you don't like your older sister,

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:02.010
weren't you?

00:07:06.630 --> 00:07:08.900
She has no sense of humor.

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:11.520
She might not survive in England.

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:14.200
We have to be straight with her,
or she won't understand.

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:15.830
You're right.

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:17.660
It's okay.

00:07:18.030 --> 00:07:20.520
As long as you're honest,
I'm sure she'll understand.

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:22.320
Youko's a simpleminded idiot.

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:25.080
If I could do that,
I wouldn't have this problem!

00:07:25.570 --> 00:07:27.050
She responded to herself...

00:07:32.110 --> 00:07:35.090
That's unusual... Youko really looks down.

00:07:35.090 --> 00:07:37.750
Youko, cheer up!

00:07:37.750 --> 00:07:40.590
They didn't really mean it!

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:42.840
I know, but...

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:44.060
Hang on.

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:46.750
Take this, and do this...

00:07:46.750 --> 00:07:49.630
Look! It's your favorite, manga meat!

00:07:49.630 --> 00:07:50.600
You can eat it!

00:07:50.600 --> 00:07:52.160
Now you're just mocking me!

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:57.450
I'm an only child, so I wish

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:58.900
I had siblings to fight with.

00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:01.610
What? To fight with?

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:03.410
Would you like to try it, then?

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:05.830
I'll play the older sister.

00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:07.950
I'll be the younger sister!

00:08:07.950 --> 00:08:09.460
Here we go!

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:13.710
Darn it, Onee-chan!
I'm not talking to you anymore!

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:20.690
I'm sorry! Please forgive me!

00:08:20.690 --> 00:08:22.440
I'm begging you!

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:24.440
This isn't quite what I imagined...

00:08:23.420 --> 00:08:26.080
Karen-sama! I'll do anything!

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:28.870
I'm still not going to forgive you!

00:08:28.870 --> 00:08:31.620
I'm sorry, Karen-sama!

00:08:30.020 --> 00:08:31.040
How wonderful...

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:32.960
You're jealous?

00:08:31.620 --> 00:08:33.400
Please forgive me!

00:08:32.960 --> 00:08:34.660
Are you an only child?

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:37.440
I wish I had a blonde younger sister...

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:39.030
That's what you envy?

00:08:49.530 --> 00:08:51.340
Sorry, but I'm heading home.

00:08:51.340 --> 00:08:52.810
Tell the others, okay?

00:08:52.810 --> 00:08:55.440
Okay, take care.

00:09:00.330 --> 00:09:02.860
Kouta. Mitsuki. Let's go home.

00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:03.800
Onee-chan...

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:05.760
Sorry about earlier.

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:08.770
We really do love you.

00:09:12.040 --> 00:09:14.300
No, don't be happy.

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:15.960
They could be lying again.

00:09:15.960 --> 00:09:17.950
She doesn't trust people anymore...

00:09:20.590 --> 00:09:22.170
We're not lying.

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:24.960
Really?

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:26.820
I see!

00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:28.740
Aw, jeez, you two!

00:09:28.740 --> 00:09:30.440
I love you, too!

00:09:30.440 --> 00:09:31.010
Hey...

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:35.250
I can sympathize with Aya-oneechan.

00:09:35.250 --> 00:09:36.350
Me, too.

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:38.590
Why are you talking about Aya?

00:09:42.570 --> 00:09:46.440
<i>How can I be honest about how I feel?</i>

00:09:49.930 --> 00:09:52.650
Aya-chan, is something wrong?

00:09:54.340 --> 00:09:57.270
It's hard to tell the truth...

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:04.800
Does that mean you're always lying?

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:07.660
Are you actually a master of jokes?

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:10.410
You're not actually English, are you?

00:10:10.410 --> 00:10:12.410
Teach me, master!

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:14.290
N-No, I'm not!

00:10:14.570 --> 00:10:17.040
I'm not!

00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:21.040
Hello!!
Kin-iro Mosaic

00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:24.630
Hello!!
Kin-iro Mosaic

00:10:28.430 --> 00:10:32.440
<i>I wish I could be more honest
with Youko about my feelings...</i>

00:10:33.410 --> 00:10:35.390
Morning, Aya!

00:10:36.460 --> 00:10:37.460
Morning.

00:10:37.460 --> 00:10:39.580
You always get here so early.

00:10:47.780 --> 00:10:51.180
<i>Youko, your smile is like the sun.</i>

00:10:52.680 --> 00:10:54.050
<i>How embarrassing!</i>

00:10:55.390 --> 00:10:58.240
<i>B-But today, I'm going to be honest!</i>

00:10:58.240 --> 00:11:01.690
Y-Youko... You're like the sun.

00:11:03.960 --> 00:11:06.670
Huh? What does that mean?

00:11:06.670 --> 00:11:08.660
I'm so intense, I suffocate you?

00:11:10.380 --> 00:11:12.700
<i>I give up!</i>

00:11:13.570 --> 00:11:14.790
<i>What's with her?</i>

00:11:16.970 --> 00:11:18.690
Good morning.

00:11:18.690 --> 00:11:20.710
Sorry we're late.

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:22.440
Morning, Shino.

00:11:22.440 --> 00:11:23.460
Morning.

00:11:23.810 --> 00:11:24.680
You too, Alice.

00:11:24.680 --> 00:11:25.970
Good morning, woof.

00:11:27.770 --> 00:11:29.720
Alice, really...

00:11:29.720 --> 00:11:30.430
Woof, woof.

00:11:30.680 --> 00:11:31.510
Woof.

00:11:32.890 --> 00:11:34.640
No, Alice!

00:11:34.640 --> 00:11:36.590
You can't tempt me.

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:39.600
You want a dog?

00:11:39.600 --> 00:11:43.150
Yes. We saw some dogs on TV last night.

00:11:43.150 --> 00:11:45.320
I want to cuddle one.

00:11:45.770 --> 00:11:49.190
Alice has a big dog in England.

00:11:49.190 --> 00:11:50.410
So that's why.

00:11:50.810 --> 00:11:52.790
You won't let her have one?

00:11:52.790 --> 00:11:56.050
I think small dogs are cute,

00:11:56.050 --> 00:12:00.420
but all dogs seem to bark at me.

00:12:01.540 --> 00:12:02.420
See?

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:04.090
Why?!

00:12:04.090 --> 00:12:05.050
Stop that!

00:12:05.050 --> 00:12:06.390
I'm sorry.

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:10.010
Maybe they don't take you seriously.

00:12:10.680 --> 00:12:11.930
I know!

00:12:11.930 --> 00:12:15.770
Why don't you visit someone
who has a dog, and play with it?

00:12:16.030 --> 00:12:17.310
Oh, good idea.

00:12:17.610 --> 00:12:20.470
Then I can cuddle a dog
without ever owning one.

00:12:20.470 --> 00:12:23.530
One of Shino's neighbors
has a dog, don't they?

00:12:27.870 --> 00:12:29.780
Huh? What is it?

00:12:29.780 --> 00:12:31.700
What about you, Karen?

00:12:31.700 --> 00:12:33.450
I have a turtle.

00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:36.910
You can't cuddle a turtle.

00:12:37.890 --> 00:12:38.920
Really?

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:42.580
<i>I got her hopes up and let her down!</i>

00:12:43.140 --> 00:12:46.170
L-Let me introduce you to my pet!

00:12:46.170 --> 00:12:47.050
Huh?!

00:12:47.360 --> 00:12:49.010
Wh-Wh-Wha—

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:51.140
<i>Youko sees me as a pet?!</i>

00:12:51.140 --> 00:12:54.620
Don't get the wrong idea, Aya!
Just hear me out.

00:12:54.620 --> 00:12:56.660
In middle school...

00:13:01.920 --> 00:13:04.640
<i>Aya looks just like a puppy.</i>

00:13:05.300 --> 00:13:08.660
<i>I wish I could put a collar on
her and take her for a walk.</i>

00:13:09.410 --> 00:13:11.540
That's a thought I had once.

00:13:12.090 --> 00:13:14.400
Y-Youko, I had no idea...

00:13:15.050 --> 00:13:17.640
you were such a pervert!

00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:20.330
No, Youko-chan.

00:13:20.660 --> 00:13:23.530
That's not a bad idea. I think I'll steal it.

00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:27.530
Alice, starting today, I will be your dog.

00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:28.470
What?

00:13:28.840 --> 00:13:31.500
I'll shake hands and go on walks.

00:13:31.500 --> 00:13:32.140
But...

00:13:32.140 --> 00:13:35.220
Give me any command you like!

00:13:37.850 --> 00:13:40.660
I don't want to see you like this!

00:13:40.660 --> 00:13:42.860
Alice... But why?

00:13:43.160 --> 00:13:44.860
That's to be expected.

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:50.360
I'm out of power...

00:13:51.050 --> 00:13:51.860
Huh?

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:53.190
Alice!

00:13:53.190 --> 00:13:54.960
Hang in there!

00:13:56.820 --> 00:13:57.930
Poppy...

00:13:57.930 --> 00:13:58.960
Oh, no!

00:13:58.960 --> 00:14:01.780
Alice's cuddle-craving meter is maxed out!

00:14:03.670 --> 00:14:05.180
What should we do?

00:14:05.670 --> 00:14:07.710
As I close my eyes,

00:14:07.710 --> 00:14:12.180
I can remember Poppy's soft fur...

00:14:13.940 --> 00:14:15.510
Poppy is the name of

00:14:15.510 --> 00:14:18.260
Alice's dog in England.

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:19.620
Oh, I know!

00:14:20.060 --> 00:14:23.150
Maybe Youko's hair can stand in for Poppy.

00:14:23.150 --> 00:14:24.080
Why?

00:14:24.080 --> 00:14:25.980
Good idea, Ayaya.

00:14:26.370 --> 00:14:27.270
H-Hey...

00:14:30.650 --> 00:14:32.030
It's totally different...

00:14:32.030 --> 00:14:33.910
That hurts, somehow!

00:14:33.910 --> 00:14:35.310
Why?!

00:14:34.450 --> 00:14:35.310
Poppy...

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:36.790
But her hair is cuddly!

00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:38.710
How heartwarming.

00:14:39.010 --> 00:14:40.980
They're like elementary school kids.

00:14:40.980 --> 00:14:44.010
But it looks like something's
really bothering Alice-san.

00:14:44.490 --> 00:14:48.030
Kuzehashi-sensei, could you hold this?

00:14:48.030 --> 00:14:50.170
What? O-Oh, sure...

00:14:50.460 --> 00:14:53.740
As her teacher, I want to help her!

00:14:54.240 --> 00:14:54.800
Huh?

00:14:55.580 --> 00:14:57.480
You're willing to go that far?

00:14:58.880 --> 00:15:00.350
Woof, woof!

00:15:01.350 --> 00:15:02.730
That sounds like Poppy...

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:04.380
That perked her up a little.

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:05.400
Woof! Woof!

00:15:05.650 --> 00:15:07.270
Woof!

00:15:08.940 --> 00:15:12.060
<i>Sensei, way to go!</i>

00:15:12.060 --> 00:15:13.780
<i>I must learn from her.</i>

00:15:14.790 --> 00:15:15.920
I see.

00:15:15.920 --> 00:15:19.030
So Alice-san had a dog in England, huh?

00:15:19.600 --> 00:15:23.410
Karasuma-sensei, you have a rabbit, don't you?

00:15:23.410 --> 00:15:24.330
That's right.

00:15:24.950 --> 00:15:27.820
Kuzehashi-sensei, do you have any pets?

00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:28.670
I...

00:15:29.010 --> 00:15:30.300
She has a kitty.

00:15:30.810 --> 00:15:33.650
She has a picture of it
as her cell's wallpaper.

00:15:33.650 --> 00:15:35.170
Karasuma-sensei!

00:15:35.170 --> 00:15:37.360
Not in front of the students!

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:38.660
My dignity...

00:15:38.660 --> 00:15:39.430
Huh?

00:15:41.990 --> 00:15:46.440
Some people really soften
up around animals.

00:15:46.440 --> 00:15:50.440
My father pets our turtle's
shell all the time.

00:15:52.360 --> 00:15:55.230
Alice-chan, I'm back.

00:15:55.790 --> 00:15:57.960
Were you lonely here by yourself?

00:15:57.450 --> 00:15:59.740
Alice = Rabbit's Name

00:15:57.960 --> 00:15:59.960
Let's eat.

00:16:00.820 --> 00:16:01.950
Listen to this...

00:16:01.950 --> 00:16:04.700
Today, I got cookies from a student.

00:16:06.390 --> 00:16:07.400
Ahem.

00:16:07.400 --> 00:16:08.710
Sensei?

00:16:15.470 --> 00:16:20.230
I must have driven you all crazy
today with my selfishness.

00:16:20.230 --> 00:16:21.330
I'm sorry.

00:16:21.550 --> 00:16:23.440
Don't sweat it.

00:16:23.440 --> 00:16:26.350
Why don't you try asking for a pet again?

00:16:26.350 --> 00:16:29.600
But I'm just here on a homestay.

00:16:29.970 --> 00:16:33.970
Caring for pets is good for
children's emotional development.

00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:37.970
I'm sure it will help you mature, too.

00:16:38.630 --> 00:16:40.370
Stare...

00:16:41.340 --> 00:16:44.650
Youko, we're the same age.

00:16:44.650 --> 00:16:46.570
Are you treating me like a child?

00:16:47.130 --> 00:16:48.620
I-I know that!

00:16:49.260 --> 00:16:52.630
Shino, listen to this!

00:16:53.100 --> 00:16:56.890
Caring for pets is good for
children's emotional development!

00:16:57.350 --> 00:16:58.390
Do you see?

00:16:59.510 --> 00:17:00.910
All right.

00:17:01.260 --> 00:17:04.260
If a dog is properly trained, it won't bark.

00:17:04.740 --> 00:17:07.060
Let's ask my family.

00:17:07.490 --> 00:17:09.440
Maybe they'll let us have one.

00:17:10.030 --> 00:17:11.440
Shino!

00:17:11.440 --> 00:17:13.870
Shino, you're always shining,

00:17:13.870 --> 00:17:16.320
but today, you're as bright as the sun!

00:17:17.530 --> 00:17:19.420
Oh, I'm not really...

00:17:25.140 --> 00:17:27.830
<i>Alice can say it so naturally...</i>

00:17:28.380 --> 00:17:29.990
A pet, huh?

00:17:31.340 --> 00:17:33.710
Aya, is there any animal
you'd want as a pet?

00:17:33.710 --> 00:17:34.960
Well...

00:17:35.750 --> 00:17:36.590
Maybe a bird...

00:17:36.900 --> 00:17:39.110
Get your grilled chicken here!

00:17:39.820 --> 00:17:41.820
Grilled... chicken...

00:17:41.820 --> 00:17:44.100
Sorry, that was awful timing!

00:17:44.350 --> 00:17:45.920
A bird sounds nice.

00:17:45.920 --> 00:17:49.040
Thanks, but...

00:17:49.550 --> 00:17:51.260
I don't need any pets.

00:17:51.710 --> 00:17:52.600
Why not?

00:17:53.050 --> 00:17:54.040
Because...

00:17:54.770 --> 00:17:58.260
<i>Now's the time. Be honest and natural...</i>

00:17:58.650 --> 00:18:02.610
I don't need pets because I have
all of my friends... and you, Youko.

00:18:05.070 --> 00:18:08.040
I-I've got something I need
to do, so I'd better go!

00:18:08.040 --> 00:18:09.270
See you later!

00:18:10.340 --> 00:18:12.010
<i>I'm so embarrassed!</i>

00:18:12.530 --> 00:18:15.440
<i>But I was honest and direct, right?</i>

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:20.860
Does that mean I'm a pet?

00:18:21.280 --> 00:18:22.990
Was she getting me back for earlier?

00:18:25.350 --> 00:18:26.600
A pet?

00:18:27.070 --> 00:18:28.330
No way.

00:18:28.330 --> 00:18:31.490
They shed, they make your clothes smell,

00:18:31.490 --> 00:18:33.310
and they cost money.

00:18:33.890 --> 00:18:36.860
They're cute enough on TV.

00:18:37.190 --> 00:18:38.490
Look, doggies.

00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:40.340
Don't say that.

00:18:40.340 --> 00:18:43.490
Please! It's for Alice!

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:46.410
No. Means. No.

00:18:50.420 --> 00:18:53.120
Th-This is all I can do.

00:18:53.120 --> 00:18:54.470
I'm sorry.

00:18:54.470 --> 00:18:56.310
Isami is so strong!

00:19:03.540 --> 00:19:04.890
Poppy?

00:19:07.470 --> 00:19:08.880
A stuffed toy?

00:19:11.390 --> 00:19:13.130
I made it.

00:19:13.430 --> 00:19:16.260
I thought it would cheer you up.

00:19:16.560 --> 00:19:18.270
Onee-chan got the vacuum.

00:19:18.270 --> 00:19:21.010
Thank you, Shino and Isami!

00:19:21.010 --> 00:19:22.650
I love it!

00:19:24.290 --> 00:19:25.530
I'm so glad.

00:19:26.780 --> 00:19:29.030
I was supposed to make a shopping run.

00:19:32.880 --> 00:19:35.600
We'll play later, Poppy.

00:19:36.850 --> 00:19:38.430
See you later.

00:19:38.430 --> 00:19:40.030
Want me to go with you?

00:19:40.030 --> 00:19:41.290
It's okay.

00:19:41.290 --> 00:19:43.440
I'm full of energy now.

00:19:43.760 --> 00:19:46.040
Watch out for cars.

00:19:46.550 --> 00:19:48.350
Do you have your handkerchief?

00:19:48.350 --> 00:19:49.370
Your wallet?

00:19:49.370 --> 00:19:52.370
Only cross when the light is green.

00:20:00.760 --> 00:20:01.940
Huh?

00:20:02.190 --> 00:20:04.420
It's Kouta-kun and Mitsuki-chan.

00:20:05.240 --> 00:20:06.890
Are you playing together?

00:20:07.310 --> 00:20:09.450
Play with us, Alice-chan.

00:20:09.450 --> 00:20:12.010
I'm on a shopping run.

00:20:12.470 --> 00:20:13.450
Sorry.

00:20:13.450 --> 00:20:15.670
Aw.

00:20:17.760 --> 00:20:19.460
Alice-chan, the truth is...

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:21.460
Mumble, mumble.

00:20:24.840 --> 00:20:26.140
Coming.

00:20:28.140 --> 00:20:29.300
Youko-chan!

00:20:29.300 --> 00:20:31.560
Is it true that when you
woke up this morning,

00:20:31.560 --> 00:20:33.570
you could speak twelve languages?

00:20:33.570 --> 00:20:34.850
We heard the news!

00:20:34.850 --> 00:20:36.100
How did you do it?

00:20:36.460 --> 00:20:39.740
I heard you became a hero
and are going on a journey!

00:20:39.740 --> 00:20:40.920
Is it true?

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:44.110
Y-Y-You didn't really
get m-married, did you?

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:46.950
What are you talking about?

00:20:46.950 --> 00:20:48.860
Everyone's here.

00:20:49.290 --> 00:20:51.740
We wanted them to play with us.

00:20:51.740 --> 00:20:53.990
You little liars!

00:21:01.160 --> 00:21:03.380
Sorry to drag you out on a weekend.

00:21:03.910 --> 00:21:06.070
Didn't you have something you had to do?

00:21:06.070 --> 00:21:07.130
It's fine.

00:21:08.990 --> 00:21:11.890
I'm glad it was a lie.

00:21:12.260 --> 00:21:13.010
Huh?

00:21:16.370 --> 00:21:18.140
Of course it was a lie.

00:21:18.140 --> 00:21:19.020
I guess so.

00:21:19.360 --> 00:21:22.520
Aya-oneechan's being honest today.

00:21:23.470 --> 00:21:24.340
Yeah.

00:22:56.990 --> 00:23:00.420
Karen, your blonde hair
is worth more than gold.

00:23:01.850 --> 00:23:03.780
<i>I still have a long way to go.</i>

00:23:03.780 --> 00:23:07.000
<i>I should compliment Youko's strengths, too.</i>

00:23:07.380 --> 00:23:10.220
<i>Her strengths, her strengths...</i>

00:23:11.340 --> 00:23:12.510
What are you looking at?

00:23:15.770 --> 00:23:18.060
D-Don't get the wrong idea!

00:23:18.060 --> 00:23:19.560
My eyes were just wandering!

00:23:19.560 --> 00:23:20.700
What?

00:23:21.430 --> 00:23:23.790
Youko, you have no dignity as an older sister.

00:23:23.790 --> 00:23:25.440
That's not true!

00:23:25.440 --> 00:23:28.330
Starting today, you'll call me "Onee-sama"!

00:23:28.190 --> 00:23:29.110
You got that?!

00:23:28.330 --> 00:23:29.350
Onee-sama...

00:23:29.350 --> 00:23:31.030
Your socks don't match.

00:23:31.030 --> 00:23:32.120
M-My dignity!

00:23:32.120 --> 00:23:33.190
You're missing your ribbon, too.

00:23:33.190 --> 00:23:34.210
I never had a ribbon!

00:23:33.190 --> 00:23:35.610
Rain or Shine

00:23:34.210 --> 00:23:35.610
See you next time!
